fix(signer): succeed a retired by-tree pointer instead of stranding the tree (#213)

A tree whose by-tree pointer named a retired run could not be committed to
again by anyone. scripts/innsegl-commit.sh handed the run to sign_commit, the
tool refused — rightly, IP §6.2 makes retirement effective immediately — and
the script had no answer to the refusal. Three separate callers hit it in one
day and all three invented the same workaround, which is a missing feature and
not a coincidence.

Re-registering is not the fix. A run id is a pure function of (agent_type,
task, idempotency_key), so asking again with the same three values derives the
same retired id and register_agent replays it; deleting the pointer does not
help, because the next derivation names the same dead run. The successor
therefore registers under a key that NAMES the run it succeeds. That makes it
distinct by construction, deterministic per (retired run, tree) so a crash
before the pointer is rewritten cannot mint a second identity for one tree
(IP §6.6), and it makes the succession a record rather than a log line:
register_agent writes the idempotency key into run_registered, so the chain
says which run this one continues. Both ids are printed, and the pointer keeps
a fourth line naming what it superseded.

A pointer naming a run this ledger never held stays a refusal. Inventing an
identity there would attribute a tree's work to a run whose own history cannot
be found, which is the opposite of what the pointer is for. An explicit -r is
never substituted either: it means that run and nothing else, and a retired one
is still refused by sign_commit, naming the run the caller named.

The liveness question is asked of the read API before sign_commit is called,
and a probe that could not run is reported as exactly that rather than treated
as a retirement — the wider version of this same bug.

Driven by OPS-037 and OPS-038 in the new scripts/innsegl-commit-selftest.sh,
written and watched failing first, and by OPS-039 against the live stack: a
genuinely retired run, this commit signed under its successor.

